  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-101(b-1)(2)): “Convicted of a disqualifying crime” does not include a case in which a person received a probation before judgment: (i) for assault in the second degree, UNLESS THE CRIME WAS A DOMESTICALLY RELATED CRIME AS DEFINED IN § 6–233 OF THE CRIMINAL PROCEDURE ARTICLE; or (ii) that was expunged under Title 10, Subtitle 1 of the Criminal Procedure Article."
